{
  "decision": "infeasible",
  "rationale": "The throughput constraint (>= 32 MSPS) is unreachable for any family in the registry. The iterative and unrolled_k families, which were exhaustively explored in the previous round, have a maximum observed throughput of 10.9 MSPS, which is less than 35% of the required 32 MSPS. Even if the pipelined families (which produce 1 result/cycle) were explored, the system constraint sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.5 us is also unreachable. The system issues 32 requests at once every 1 us. To meet the 0.5 us batch latency, the CORDIC must process all 32 requests in 0.5 us. This requires a throughput of at least 64 MSPS (32 requests / 0.5 us). The best throughput seen so far is 10.9 MSPS, which is far below the 64 MSPS required to satisfy the system batch latency constraint. Therefore, no design in the registry can meet the constraints."
